```server-java
import io.appwrite.Client;
import io.appwrite.coroutines.CoroutineCallback;
import io.appwrite.exceptions.AppwriteException;
import io.appwrite.enums.VideoOutput;
import io.appwrite.services.Videos;

Client client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint("https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1")
    .setProject("<PROJECT_ID>")
    .setKey("<API_KEY>");

Videos videos = new Videos(client);

try {
    videos.createRendition(
        "<VIDEO_ID>", // videoId
        "<PROFILE_ID>", // profileId
        VideoOutput.CMAF, // output
        new CoroutineCallback<>((result, error) -> {
            if (error != null) {
                error.printStackTrace();
                return;
            }

            System.out.println(result);
        })
    );
} catch (AppwriteException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

```server-rust
use appwrite::Client;
use appwrite::enums::VideoOutput;
use appwrite::services::Videos;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = Client::new();
    client.set_endpoint("https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1");
    client.set_project("<PROJECT_ID>");
    client.set_key("<API_KEY>");

    let videos = Videos::new(&client);

    let rendition = videos.create_rendition(
        "<VIDEO_ID>",
        "<PROFILE_ID>",
        VideoOutput::Cmaf
    ).await?;

    println!("{:?}", rendition);

    Ok(())
}
```

```http
POST /v1/videos/<VIDEO_ID>/renditions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Appwrite-Project: <PROJECT_ID>
X-Appwrite-Key: <API_KEY>

{
  "profileId": "<PROFILE_ID>",
  "output": "cmaf"
}
```
{% /multicode %}

Encoding starts in the background as soon as the rendition is created. You can create renditions right after the video, before its metadata is probed.

Renditions encode independently, so the video can start streaming as soon as the first one is ready. Players see more qualities as more renditions finish. To get something on screen fast, create the lower profiles first.

Encoding time depends mostly on the source duration and the profile's resolution. A 2160p rendition takes many times longer than a 480p one of the same clip.

You can create up to 15 renditions per video per hour. Past that, `videos.createRendition()` returns a `general_rate_limit_exceeded` error until the hour is up.

The profile's codec must support the output you ask for. H.264, the only codec available today, supports all three.

# Status and progress {% #status-and-progress %}

A rendition reports its `status` and a `progress` percentage while it encodes.

{% only_dark %}
![Renditions tab with two renditions queued and the 360p rendition encoding, with a progress bar for each](/images/docs/videos/dark/renditions-encoding.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Renditions tab with two renditions queued and the 360p rendition encoding, with a progress bar for each](/images/docs/videos/renditions-encoding.avif)
{% /only_light %}

| Status | Console label | Meaning |
|--------|---------------|---------|
| `pending` | Queued | Waiting for an encoding worker |
| `started` | Encoding | Transcoding the source |
| `ended` | Encoded | Transcoding finished. Segments and manifests are being stored |
| `ready` | Ready | Included in the master manifest and ready to stream |
| `error` | Failed | The encode failed |
| `aborted` | Aborted | The encode made no progress for 12 hours and was stopped |

Each rendition also records `startedAt` and `endedAt`, its `width`, `height`, bitrates, and `codec`, and `targetDuration`, the length of its longest segment in seconds. When a rendition fails or is aborted, `error` says why.

`progress` is an integer percentage from 0 to 100, such as `42`.

# Wait until ready {% #wait-until-ready %}

The Console updates rendition progress live. In your own backend, list the video's renditions with [queries](/docs/products/databases/tablesdb/queries) on `status` and `output`. The video can stream once `total` is greater than 0:

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
const sdk = require('node-appwrite');

const client = new sdk.Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')
    .setKey('<API_KEY>');

const videos = new sdk.Videos(client);

const renditions = await videos.listRenditions({
    videoId: '<VIDEO_ID>',
    queries: [sdk.Query.equal('output', ['cmaf']), sdk.Query.equal('status', ['ready'])] // optional
});
```

```server-python
from appwrite.client import Client
from appwrite.services.videos import Videos
from appwrite.query import Query

client = Client()
client.set_endpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
client.set_project('<PROJECT_ID>')
client.set_key('<API_KEY>')

videos = Videos(client)

renditions = videos.list_renditions(
    video_id = '<VIDEO_ID>',
    queries = [Query.equal('output', ['cmaf']), Query.equal('status', ['ready'])] # optional
)
```

